--- !u!114 &187775719
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 187775715}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 31b2213fa83bf654b8bcfdd24c62192a, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  noteImage: {fileID: 939777222}
  noteText: {fileID: 1457762497}
  nextButton: {fileID: 2077385133}
  prevButton: {fileID: 1155710528}
  notes:
  - image: {fileID: 21300000, guid: e7319c500fa3dff4fbfb0fa24007643d, type: 3}
    text: The "Six-Pack" is the primary flight instrument cluster, providing essential
      flight data. These instruments help pilots maintain control, monitor altitude,
      and navigate safely.
  - image: {fileID: 21300000, guid: efddc1894b3d3704c88508441a3344ea, type: 3}
    text: "Circuit breakers are safety features that protect the aircraft\u2019s
      electrical components from overloads, ensuring system reliability during flight."
  - image: {fileID: 21300000, guid: eb66b9cf479c8004286bdd09fe60501f, type: 3}
    text: These systems allow pilots to communicate with air traffic control, follow
      designated flight paths, and enhance situational awareness in various flight
      conditions.
  - image: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 8055156fed5985e47b165a249b240de6, type: 3}
    text: The throttle controls engine power, while the mixture adjusts the fuel-to-air
      ratio for optimal engine performance. The flap lever is used to increase lift
      and drag during landing and takeoff, helping pilots manage airspeed and descent
      rates efficiently.
  - image: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 2679713cbb8c3b1408c2d46c8c326ff3, type: 3}
    text: The trim wheel helps relieve control pressure for smoother flight handling.
      The fuel shutoff valve allows pilots to cut off fuel flow in emergencies. The
      fuel selector switch enables switching between tanks, ensuring balanced fuel
      distribution and preventing fuel starvation during flight.
